; Where each frame is in its sentence's fall to the end. Four cards a frame in: whether it starts a sentence (from
; sents) and its sentence's to, M and end (from spread); per frame two cards out: y, how far into the fall in
; hundredths (-1 before frame to, or with no fall), and the end (1 a statement, 2 a question). y = 100 (f - to) / M
; by Bresenham: each frame past to adds 100 to yr and takes M away as often as it goes; at most 100.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            frm     INP   ns       03-12: a frame; a new sentence starts f and y again
  04                    INP   to
  05                    INP   m
  06                    INP   end
  07                    CLA   ns
  08                    SUB   00
  09                    TAC   go
  10                    CLA   z
  11                    STO   f
  12                    STO   y
  13                    STO   yr
  14            go      CLA   to       14-25: y (or -1) and the end out
  15                    TAC   none
  16                    CLA   f
  17                    SUB   to
  18                    TAC   none
  19                    OUT   y
  20                    JMP   nx
  21            none    OUT   m1
  22            nx      OUT   end
  23                    CLA   f
  24                    ADD   00
  25                    STO   f
  26                    CLA   to       26-52: y on a frame, past to
  27                    TAC   frm
  28                    CLA   to
  29                    SUB   f
  30                    TAC   yu
  31                    JMP   frm
  32            yu      CLA   y
  33                    SUB   c100
  34                    TAC   yg
  35                    JMP   frm
  36            yg      CLA   yr
  37                    ADD   c100
  38                    STO   yr
  39            yl      CLA   yr
  40                    SUB   m
  41                    TAC   yc
  42                    STO   yr
  43                    CLA   y
  44                    ADD   00
  45                    STO   y
  46                    JMP   yl
  47            yc      CLA   y
  48                    SUB   c100
  49                    TAC   frm
  50                    CLA   c100
  51                    STO   y
  52                    JMP   frm
  70            ns      DATA  0
  71            to      DATA  0
  72            m       DATA  0
  73            end     DATA  0
  74            f       DATA  0
  75            y       DATA  0
  76            yr      DATA  0
  77            z       DATA  0
  78            m1      DATA  -1
  79            c100    DATA  100
